    <h2>1. What is HTML? The Full Form and Meaning</h2>
    <p><b>HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.</b> It is the standard language used to create the structure of every website on the internet. When you open Google, YouTube, Facebook, or any website, you are looking at HTML first.</p>
    <p>HTML is not a programming language. It is a markup language. That means it does not do calculations or logic. It only tells the browser what to show and where to show it. For example, HTML tells the browser, this is a heading, this is a paragraph, this is an image, and this is a button.</p>
    <p>Think of HTML as the <b>skeleton of a website</b>. Just like a human body needs a skeleton to stand, a website needs HTML to stand. Without HTML, there is no website. CSS is used later to make that skeleton beautiful with colors and design, and JavaScript is used to make it interactive.</p>
    <h2>2. Why Should You Learn HTML in 2026?</h2>
    <p>Learning HTML is the first step to becoming a web developer. It is the easiest language to learn, and you do not need any previous experience. If you can type in English, you can learn HTML. Many students, shop owners, and job seekers learn HTML to create their own websites, portfolios, and online stores.</p>
    <p>Once you learn HTML, you can easily learn CSS, JavaScript, and then get freelance work or a job. Even if you want to start a blog or a business website, basic HTML will save you a lot of money.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>In simple words:</b><br>Everything you see on a website - headings, paragraphs, buttons, images, forms - is made with HTML. CSS makes it beautiful, but first you must learn HTML.</div>
    <h2>3. What Do You Need to Learn HTML?</h2>
    <p>You need only two free things to start learning HTML:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>VS Code</b> - A free code editor to write your HTML code. You can download it from the internet for free.</li>
      <li><b>A Browser</b> - Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge to see your website.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>That is it. No money is needed. You can learn HTML on a mobile phone, laptop, or computer.</p>
    <h2>4. How Does HTML Work?</h2>
    <p>HTML works with tags. A tag is a special word inside angle brackets, like <b>&lt;h1&gt;</b> or <b>&lt;p&gt;</b>. Most tags come in pairs: an opening tag and a closing tag. For example, <b>&lt;h1&gt;Hello&lt;/h1&gt;</b> means show Hello as a big heading.</p>
    <p>When you save your code as a file with the name <b>index.html</b> and open it in a browser, the browser reads your HTML tags and shows the result on the screen. That is how every website works.</p>
    <h2>5. Your First Website - Example Code</h2>
    <p>Copy the code below, save it in VS Code as <b>index.html</b>, and double-click to open it in your browser:</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code><span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br><span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br><span class="tag">&lt;head&gt;</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;title&gt;</span><span class="text">My First Website</span><span class="tag">&lt;/title&gt;</span><br><span class="tag">&lt;/head&gt;</span><br><span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">Hello World!</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">This is my first website, I made it myself.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br><span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span><br><span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span></code></div>
    <h2>6. The Result Will Look Like This:</h2>
    <div class="result"><h1>Hello World!</h1><p>This is my first website, I made it myself.</p></div>
    <div class="box"><b>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</b> = Tells the browser this is an HTML file.<br><br><b>&lt;html&gt;</b> = The whole website is inside this tag.<br><br><b>&lt;head&gt;</b> = Title and hidden information which is not visible on the page.<br><br><b>&lt;body&gt;</b> = Everything visible on the page is inside this tag.<br><br><b>&lt;h1&gt;</b> = The biggest heading on the page.<br><br><b>&lt;p&gt;</b> = Paragraph or normal text.</div>
    <h2>7. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>Now make your first website with your own name. Change the heading and paragraph to your own words. This small practice will give you confidence to continue to the next lesson, where you will learn about headings and paragraphs in detail.</p>
